839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050986 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "772caedd-5534-5223-bec5-a96cc56f64c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186181421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181416 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "82513cd4-0854-5641-b6b1-efbbfd7c3b1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181417 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{14}{125}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181417 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181417 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9a9cefb8-a0e4-5b79-8c26-5ac76834bb3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181418 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181418 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181418 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b8927739-bda7-5c7d-9801-ca342ae0aebf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181419 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{11}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2cf2677-bb1c-5019-88a5-62130e41078a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181420 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{11}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181420 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eeb88dbe-2a14-5a9b-a7a2-c04f09113dd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181421 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{44}{125}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181421 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186181421 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5fb9827b-2023-5742-96d5-5dadfc0ba955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184053 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184053 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin u = -\\dfrac {4} {5}, \\qquad\n\\cos v = \\dfrac {15} {17}, \\qquad\n\\sin v = \\dfrac {8} {17}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, find the value of $\\cos\\left(u + v\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184053 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5da3337e-31d2-5f2d-b236-60088b4bf64d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184053 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u + v) = \\cos u \\cos v - \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{u}$, $\\cos{v}$, and $\\sin{v}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{u,}$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 u + \\cos^2 u= 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 u = 1- \\sin^2 u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{4}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\cos u= -\\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{15}{17})-(-\\frac{4}{5})(\\frac{8}{17}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{85}+\\frac{32}{85} \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{85}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184135 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184135 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\sin u = \\dfrac {4} {5}, \\qquad\n\\cos u = \\dfrac {3} {5}, \\qquad \n\\sin v = \\dfrac {9} {15}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\cos\\left(u - v\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184135 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8877f6b8-8914-5022-9ec6-d4e8e0d3d159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184135 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{u}$, $\\cos{u}$, and $\\sin{v}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{v,}$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 v + \\cos^2 v= 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 v = 1- \\sin^2 v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{9}{15})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{9}^{2}}{{15}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{81}{225} \\\\  & =\\frac{225}{225}-\\frac{81}{225} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{225}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{144}{225}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{12}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\cos v= \\dfrac{12}{15}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{12}{15})+(\\frac{4}{5})(\\frac{9}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{75}+\\frac{36}{75} \\\\  & =\\frac{72}{75} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184143 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184143 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186184540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184143 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186184827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184143 #edb/r